Lab: Design a SOHO Network

Objective

Designing a new SOHO network using the network modeler.

Environment

Tools Used

Terminal
Network Modeler

Operating System

Windows 10 Enterprise
Windows 11 Pro

Skills Practiced

SOHO Network Design
Network Topology
Device Connectivity
DHCP Configuration
Network Connectivity Testing

Actions Performed

1. I logged in to the lab. The canvas was blank. In the End Devices tray, I added two PCs and a Laptop to the canvas.
2. Under the Switch icon, I added a switch to the canvas. 
3. Under the Router icon, I added a router to the canvas. 
4. Utilizing the Create Link button, I connected the Router, Port 0, to the Switch, Port 0.
5. Connected both desktop PCs and the laptop to Switch Ports 1, 2, and 3 using the Create Link tool. 
6. Verified all network connections were complete and correctly displayed in the Network Modeler. 
7. I then launch Windows on PC1. I open the Network & Internet tab in settings. I verify that the IP and DNS settings are set to Automatic. 
8. Opened an administrative terminal and verified network connectivity by pinging the external DNS server.
9. I confirmed connectivity on the other PC and laptop using the same procedure as above. 
10. Documented findings and ended lab

Commands Used

ping 192.168.1.1

Verification

I verified all devices were placed on the canvas and connected properly. After I completed verification on the modeler, I ensured every End Device DHCP and DNS were set to automatic and pinged the external DNS Server. The ping command verified that every device was properly connected.

Issues Encountered

None

Resolution

Successfully designed and verified a small SOHO network using the Network Modeler. Connected all end devices, confirmed DHCP and DNS settings, and verified network connectivity using the ping command. 

Key Takeaways

- A switch provides local network connectivity between end devices.
- A router connects the local network to external networks.
- DHCP simplifies client configuration by automatically assigning IP settings.
- Connectivity should always be verified after network deployment.
- The ping command is a quick method for validating basic network communication.

